From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 12:49:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200038=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?SB16=20IRQ-5=20instrumentation=20+=20idle-pause?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Companion to patch 0037 (audio synth helpers + public-API state).
This patch wires the SB16 audio backend's IRQ-5 path to:
  1. Bracket each IRQ entry/exit with BIOS-tick timing for the
     `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us` cumulative wall-clock counter.
  2. Increment `doskutsu_audio_irq_count` per IRQ.
  3. Increment `doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count` when ring contains
     non-silence content (semantically: SFX-active under WB/OPL3
     backend; degenerates to ~ irq_count under Organya per
     docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md cross-PLAY ablation framing).
  4. Track consecutive-silent-IRQs; when threshold met (4 IRQs ~92 ms
     at 43 Hz IRQ rate) AND idle-pause enabled, signal pause request
     to non-IRQ service path.
  5. Service pause/resume requests in WaitDevice and PlayDevice from
     non-IRQ context; issue DSP commands 0xD5 / 0xD6 (16-bit) or
     0xD0 / 0xD4 (8-bit) per soundblaster_is_sb16; fire registered
     idle-pause callback at resume with measured paused_ns.

Per audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md (W20A2 ablation finding):
the IRQ entry/exit wall-clock itself is ~13.5 ms / flip on real HW;
DSP-pause suppresses the IRQ entirely during silent gameplay,
removing that cost without IDT modification (per docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md
sec. E.7 framing -- DSP pause vs IRQ unhook).

IRQ-handler timing uses BIOS tick at 0040:006C (atomic single-bus-cycle
far peek; guaranteed IRQ-safe; no DPMI, no function call). Resolution
is coarse (~55 ms per tick) but cumulative-mean over many IRQs
converges to true wall-clock at the us-aggregate granularity the
contract requires.

ISR variables locked alongside existing isr_* state at OpenDevice:
  isr_consecutive_silent_irqs, isr_dsp_paused, idle-pause flags +
  callback pointer, doskutsu_audio_* counters.

Per CLAUDE.md threading-zero invariant: no threads. Pause/resume
requests are flag-driven; serviced synchronously from WaitDevice
loop and PlayDevice path. ForcePause/ForceResume helpers in
patch 0037 set the same flags for ablation testing.

Risk per sdl3_dos_quirks.md PR #15377 author note: DSP pause
behavior on real Vibra16S CT2490 untested. Failure-mode-graceful
per sec. E.7: if pause command doesn't take effect, IRQs keep firing
(worst case = same as Phase 9 baseline). Validation iter
(W22-WB-A) measures `audio_irq_count` delta between baseline and
WB/OPL3 backends to confirm idle-pause actually suppressed IRQs.

Engine-side counter readers in nxengine slot 0100 (already in tree
post-0099 wave-23.7 closure) resolve cleanly against the externs
defined in patch 0037.

Patch 0038 modifies vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c only;
no new files.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 174 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 174 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 327260a8b..7f44cbfc6 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -23,9 +23,24 @@
 #ifdef SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_DOS_SOUNDBLASTER
 
 #include "../../core/dos/SDL_dos.h"
+#include "../../core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h"
 #include "../../core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.h"
 #include "SDL_dosaudio_sb.h"
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): IRQ-5 instrumentation +
+   idle-pause coordination state. The public-API state vars are defined
+   in SDL_dos_audio_synth.c (patch 0037); we access them as externs and
+   service the request flags + DSP pause/resume command issuing here so
+   all DSP-port mechanics stay co-located in this audio backend.
+
+   See docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md sec. E.2 / sec. E.3 / sec. E.7 for the mechanism
+   rationale (DSP-pause vs IDT-unhook framing; failure-mode-graceful
+   semantics on real Vibra16S CT2490 untested per sdl3_dos_quirks.md). */
+extern volatile bool g_dos_audio_idle_pause_enabled;
+extern volatile bool g_dos_audio_pause_request;
+extern volatile bool g_dos_audio_resume_request;
+extern SDL_DOSIdlePauseCallback g_dos_audio_idle_pause_cb;
+
 // Set to 1 to force 8-bit mono (pre-SB16) code path even on SB16 hardware.
 // Useful for testing in DOSBox which always emulates an SB16 (DSP 4.x).
 #define FORCE_SB_8BIT 0
@@ -137,6 +152,26 @@ static int resolve_ring_chunks(void)
 // ISR-cached copies of device state (avoids chasing heap pointers in IRQ context).
 static volatile int isr_irq_ack_port = 0;
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): IRQ-handler instrumentation
+   state. Memory-locked alongside the existing isr_* state at OpenDevice.
+
+   isr_consecutive_silent_irqs: count of consecutive IRQs where ring was
+     empty (filled with silence). Reset to 0 on any non-silent IRQ.
+     When >= IDLE_PAUSE_THRESHOLD AND idle-pause is enabled, the ISR
+     sets g_dos_audio_pause_request to be serviced by non-IRQ context.
+
+   IDLE_PAUSE_THRESHOLD: 4 IRQs ~ 92 ms at 43 Hz IRQ rate. Long enough
+     to avoid pausing during brief Pixtone gaps; short enough that bulk
+     silent gameplay gets the savings. Per sec. E.2 design.
+
+   Per audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md: the IRQ entry/exit wall-clock
+   ITSELF is the cost (~13.5 ms / flip on real HW). Idle-pause is the
+   mechanism to suppress IRQs entirely during silent gameplay. */
+#define IDLE_PAUSE_THRESHOLD 4
+static volatile uint32_t isr_consecutive_silent_irqs = 0;
+static volatile bool isr_dsp_paused = false; /* set/cleared by non-IRQ service path */
+static Uint64 s_dsp_pause_start_ns = 0;      /* set when pause issued; read at resume to compute paused_ns */
+
 // ISR-visible ring buffer state (all memory-locked).
 static volatile int isr_ring_read = 0;
 static volatile int isr_ring_write = 0;
@@ -190,8 +225,29 @@ static void ISR_GetDMAHalf_End(void) {}
 //
 // This function touches ONLY memory-locked data and does ONLY port I/O and
 // memcpy. No DPMI, no malloc, no mutex, no FPU.
+//
+// DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): added per-IRQ instrumentation
+// counters + silent-IRQ tracking for idle-pause coordination. Wall-clock
+// timing uses BIOS tick at 0040:006C -- atomic single-bus-cycle far peek,
+// guaranteed IRQ-safe (no DPMI, no function call, no memory allocation).
+// 1 BIOS tick = 54925 us (~54.9 ms). Per-IRQ resolution is coarse (most
+// IRQs are sub-tick); cumulative-mean over many IRQs converges to true
+// wall-clock. Sufficient for the us-aggregate `audio_irq_wall_us` counter
+// per docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md sec. 1.3.
+//
+// Per audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md: the IRQ entry/exit wall-clock
+// itself is what we're measuring; the time spent INSIDE this function is
+// a small subset. The "wall-clock" we accumulate here therefore captures
+// only the locally-observable part of the cost -- DPMI thunk overhead at
+// the wrapper-into-handler boundary is invisible to us. The contract
+// reconciles via cross-correlation with engine flip-timing.
 static void SoundBlasterIRQHandler(void)
 {
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): IRQ-handler instrumentation.
+       BIOS tick at 0040:006C is atomic + IRQ-safe; resolution coarse but
+       cumulative-mean converges. */
+    const uint32_t entry_tick = (uint32_t)_farpeekl(_dos_ds, 0x46Cul);
+
     // Acknowledge hardware first.
     inportb(isr_irq_ack_port);
     DOS_EndOfInterrupt(soundblaster_irq);
@@ -201,16 +257,101 @@ static void SoundBlasterIRQHandler(void)
     // How many bytes are available in the ring?
     const int avail = isr_ring_write - isr_ring_read; // both are monotonic
 
+    bool ring_had_audio = false;
     if (avail >= isr_chunk_size) {
         RingCopyOut(dma_dst, isr_ring_read, isr_chunk_size);
         isr_ring_read += isr_chunk_size;
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10): ring had non-silence content available.
+           Reset silent-IRQ counter; flag this IRQ as "audio active" for
+           the SFX-active counter. (Under WB/OPL3 backend, music is offloaded;
+           any ring content == SFX. Under Organya, ring always has music
+           so the counter degenerates to ~ irq_count -- semantically correct
+           for the cross-PLAY ablation per docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md.) */
+        isr_consecutive_silent_irqs = 0;
+        ring_had_audio = true;
     } else {
         // Ring underrun: fill with silence so we don't replay stale audio.
         SDL_memset(dma_dst, isr_silence_value, isr_chunk_size);
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10): consecutive-silent-IRQ tracking.
+           When threshold met AND idle-pause enabled, signal non-IRQ
+           context to issue DSP pause command. Pre-pause state is preserved
+           via single increment + atomic flag set; service path handles
+           the actual DSP command. */
+        isr_consecutive_silent_irqs++;
+        if (isr_consecutive_silent_irqs >= IDLE_PAUSE_THRESHOLD &&
+            g_dos_audio_idle_pause_enabled && !isr_dsp_paused) {
+            g_dos_audio_pause_request = true;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10): bump per-block extern counters. Single
+       32-bit volatile increment is atomic on x86 per kbd-counter
+       precedent (patches 0023+0025); engine reads via extern. */
+    doskutsu_audio_irq_count++;
+    if (ring_had_audio) {
+        doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count++;
+    }
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10): wall-clock accumulate via BIOS tick
+       delta. uint32_t modular arithmetic handles wrap (BIOS tick cycles
+       through uint32_t over ~63 hours). 1 tick = 54925 us. */
+    const uint32_t exit_tick = (uint32_t)_farpeekl(_dos_ds, 0x46Cul);
+    const uint32_t delta_ticks = exit_tick - entry_tick; /* modular */
+    if (delta_ticks > 0) {
+        doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us += delta_ticks * 54925u;
     }
 }
 static void SoundBlasterIRQHandler_End(void) {}
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): service the pause/resume request
+   flags from non-IRQ context. The IRQ handler sets g_dos_audio_pause_request
+   when consecutive silent IRQs cross the threshold; the audio writer path
+   (PlayDevice) clears it via implicit resume on next ring write. ForcePause/
+   ForceResume in patch 0037's API also set these flags. The actual DSP
+   command issuing happens here so it stays co-located with the rest of
+   the SB16 DSP-port mechanics.
+
+   DSP commands per design sec. E.2:
+     0xD5 = pause 16-bit DMA (SB16-class)
+     0xD0 = pause 8-bit DMA  (pre-SB16)
+     0xD6 = resume 16-bit DMA
+     0xD4 = resume 8-bit DMA
+
+   On pause: capture s_dsp_pause_start_ns for the resume callback's
+   paused_ns argument. On resume: compute paused_ns + fire registered
+   callback. Single-listener model; if callback is NULL, just measure
+   silently.
+
+   Note: the DSP pause behavior on real Vibra16S CT2490 is untested per
+   sdl3_dos_quirks.md PR #15377 author note. Failure-mode-graceful per
+   sec. E.7: if pause command doesn't take effect, IRQs keep firing as
+   today. Worst case = same as Phase 9 baseline. */
+static void MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests(void)
+{
+    if (g_dos_audio_resume_request) {
+        if (isr_dsp_paused) {
+            const Uint8 cmd = soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 0xD6 : 0xD4;
+            WriteSoundBlasterDSP(cmd);
+            isr_dsp_paused = false;
+            isr_consecutive_silent_irqs = 0; /* reset for next pause cycle */
+            const Uint64 paused_ns = SDL_GetTicksNS() - s_dsp_pause_start_ns;
+            if (g_dos_audio_idle_pause_cb) {
+                g_dos_audio_idle_pause_cb(paused_ns);
+            }
+        }
+        g_dos_audio_resume_request = false;
+        g_dos_audio_pause_request = false; /* resume always wins */
+        return;
+    }
+    if (g_dos_audio_pause_request && !isr_dsp_paused) {
+        const Uint8 cmd = soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 0xD5 : 0xD0;
+        s_dsp_pause_start_ns = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+        WriteSoundBlasterDSP(cmd);
+        isr_dsp_paused = true;
+        g_dos_audio_pause_request = false;
+    }
+}
+
 // Wait until the ring buffer has room for one more chunk.
 // The audio thread keeps yielding so the game's main thread can run while
 // we wait. Because the ISR is steadily draining the ring, this only blocks
@@ -221,6 +362,14 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     const int size = hidden->ring_size;
 
     for (;;) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): service pause/resume
+           requests on each WaitDevice loop iteration. Pause requests
+           come from the IRQ handler (consecutive-silent-IRQ threshold
+           met); resume requests come from PlayDevice or ForceResume.
+           Servicing here ensures DSP commands are issued from non-IRQ
+           context as required. */
+        MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
+
         // Available space = ring_size - (write - read).
         // ring_write is ours (audio thread only), ring_read is advanced by
         // the ISR. Read the ISR's copy so we see the latest drain position.
@@ -413,6 +562,20 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     DOS_LockVariable(isr_silence_value);
     DOS_LockVariable(isr_irq_ack_port);
     DOS_LockVariable(soundblaster_irq);
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): lock IRQ-handler
+       instrumentation + idle-pause coordination state. The pause
+       request flag, silent-IRQ counter, and DSP-paused flag are all
+       read or written from IRQ context. The wall-clock and count
+       counters in SDL_dos_audio_synth.c (patch 0037) are also touched
+       from IRQ context and must be locked. */
+    DOS_LockVariable(isr_consecutive_silent_irqs);
+    DOS_LockVariable(isr_dsp_paused);
+    DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_idle_pause_enabled);
+    DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_pause_request);
+    DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_resume_request);
+    DOS_LockVariable(doskutsu_audio_irq_count);
+    DOS_LockVariable(doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us);
+    DOS_LockVariable(doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count);
 
     DOS_HookInterrupt(soundblaster_irq, SoundBlasterIRQHandler, &hidden->interrupt_hook);
 
@@ -510,6 +673,17 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
     isr_ring_write = hidden->ring_write;
     DOS_EnableInterrupts();
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): if DSP is paused (no music
+       backend was streaming + ring went idle), this PlayDevice call
+       means the audio writer has fresh data to play -- almost certainly
+       a Pixtone SFX trigger. Request resume; service it now so the new
+       data starts playing immediately rather than after the next
+       WaitDevice cycle. */
+    if (isr_dsp_paused) {
+        g_dos_audio_resume_request = true;
+        MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
+    }
+
     return true;
 }
 
-- 
